     "[HKDSE 2023 Paper 1 Q5]"
    ],
    [
     "On a bus, the number of male passengers is 80% more than the number of female passengers. If\n56 male passengers get off the bus, then the number of female passengers is 80% more than the\nnumber of male passengers. Find the number of female passengers on the bus. (4 marks)\nSolution\nLet x and y be the number of female passengers and the original number of male passengers on the bus respectively.\n[IMG:image6.wmf]\nPut (1) into (2).  → To find the number of female passengers, we need to eliminate y.\nx = (1 + 80%)((1 + 80%)x – 56) (1M: for getting a linear equation in one unknown)\nx = 3.24x – 100.8\n2.24x = 100.8\nx = 45 (1A)\n∴ The number of female passengers on the bus is 45."
