     "If 8x – 9y = 30 = 4x + 3y, then y =\nA.  –3. B. –2.\nC.  2. D. 6.\nSolution\nKey Steps: • Rewrite the given equations as   two linear equations.\n• Eliminate one of the unknowns by   adding or subtracting two equations.\n• Solve the equation obtained.\n[IMG:image11.wmf]  → •\n(2) × 2: (4x + 3y) × 2 = 30 × 2\n8x + 6y = 60 …... (3)\n(3) – (1): (8x + 6y) – (8x – 9y) = 60 – 30  → •\n15y = 30\ny = 2  → →\n∴ The answer is C.",
     "The price of 3 egg tarts and 4 doughnuts is $156. If the price of 5 egg tarts and the price of 2 doughnuts are the same, then the price of an egg tart is\nA.  $12. B. $14.\nC.  $30. D. $35.\nSolution\nKey Steps: • Identify the two unknowns involved   in the question and use different  letters to represent them.\n• Set up simultaneous linear \n  equations in two unknowns.\n• Find the required unknown.\nLet $x be the price of an egg tart and \n$y be the price of a doughnut.  → •\n[IMG:image14.wmf]  → •\nFrom (2), we have [IMG:image15.wmf]\nPut (3) into (1).\n[IMG:image16.wmf] = 156\n13x = 156\nx = 12\n∴ The price of an egg tart is $12.\n∴ The answer is A."
    ]
